ousand dollars a year and whose  value in the marketplace today is over a  million dollars a year these were real  Patriots in my judgment they were there  because they believed passionately in  investor protection they believed in the  traditions of a commission that through  the years had been non partisan in its  approach to doing what was right for  America's markets and for America's  investors and they taught me a lot they  were dedicated loyal and committed  people I have a tendency to be impulsive  and I mean there are things that go on  in Washington I had a corporate  background so my background told me have  small short meetings but the  satisfaction that government employees  get is by being part of the process and  I didn't understand it at first when  when we were dealing with market  regulation the 15 people who headed that  division wanted to be in the room when a  decision was made and at first I didn't  want that to happen but I began to  understand that the compensation of  inclusiveness was far more important to  them than any amount of money that could  be paid to them and I came to feel  towards this group a an affection and a  feeling  I have not felt for any of the people  that I've ever worked with in any of my  career's I came to Washington believing  in markets to begin with and I derive  the satisfaction that I did because many  of the thoughts theories and concepts  that I embraced in my different careers  for the first time I could translate  into specific action in 1970 I gave a  speech at Columbia University while I  was the head of a firm called Shearson  Hayden stone where I cited the conflicts  of interest of brokers being paid on a  quantitative basis the conflicts of  interest in investment banking the  conflicts of interest in research my  partner said to me Arthur you're totally  impractical your Allah renzo Jones your  ideas would bankrupt us guess what I  came to the Commission with the same  ideas and I was able to implement those  ideas because they formed the basis of  an agenda that I was determined to  pursue in order to make the Commission  the most investor-friendly Commission in  the history of the agency now I said  that I believed in markets and maybe the  manifestation and an illustration of  what markets can be can best be  illustrated by another passion that I  have and that's without an endorsement I  am an absolute fanatical believer in  ebay i buy and sell hundreds of things  on ebay well about two years into the  job and my staff knew that I had this  affliction  all the men in this audience undoubtedly  have ties that you're tired of what can  you do with him you can't give them away  eventually they clog up your closet  until the point you throw them away well  not me I put up six ties on ebay for  sale now when you put something up on  ebay potential buyers send you emails  asking about do the ties have any spots  on them that's okay then I had one we  said by the way you're selling your toys  would you have a size nine and a half  brown left shoe curious and the next one  said would you have rousers to a gray  striped suit size 48 totally eccentric  the ties were sold and for a pretty good  price the next day I had six councils in  my office lawyers that worked for me and  one of them came in with some papers and  he looked vaguely familiar to me and I i  saw that tie I know that time then the  second came in and the third these guys  had all been on my ties it was the  greatest gag ever pull down  well  that's a rigged market and that's the  kind of market that we don't want to  have any part of in this country and the  SEC is there to see to it that the  market operates fairly the initiatives  that we pursued that I felt were the  most meaningful to the system included  banning the practice of pay-to-play and  again this relates to experiences that I  had when I traveled around the country  as an investment banker and went to  different communities to underwrite  